==Battleground==
*The enemy base here is a [[Relay Base (Enemy Base)|Relay Base]].
*Infinite [[Snache]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
*1 [[Hippoe]] spawns after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
*1 [[Hippoe]] spawns after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>.
*1 [[Large White Ball]] spawns after 23.33 seconds<sup>700f</sup>.
*Infinite [[White Wind]]s spawn after 25.33 seconds<sup>760f</sup>, delay 20~33.33 seconds<sup>600f~1,000f</sup>.
*1 [[Kang Roo]] spawns after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>.
*1 [[Teacher Bear]] spawns after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
*1 [[Le'boin]] spawns as the boss after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.
*1 [[Kang Roo]] spawns after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>.
*2 [[Large White Ball]]s spawn after 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This and its continuation stages are not very hard. The first continue stage, [[400m Relay: Second Fastest]] has Shy Boy, who would be hard if not for the fact that Sir Seal gives you plenty of money, and [[400m Relay: Anchor Leg]] is just One Horn with Metal Balls. All of the enemies in each stage are around 200% magnification as well. Simply spamming Normal Cats and any generalist gacha units you may have at this point should work.

For this stage specifically, [[Dragon Cat]] with meatshielding should obliterate the stage.

